{% endif %}# Writing the outcome and publishing outputs

After cherry-picking, write the result atomically to avoid races with the
orchestrator reading it:

1. First write to .test_output/{{ reducer_outcome_filename }}.draft (relative to the git repo root)
2. Then rename (mv) the .draft file to .test_output/{{ reducer_outcome_filename }}

The schema is:

{"squashed_branches": ["branch1", "branch2"],
 "squashed_commit_hash": "abc1234",
 "impl_priority": ["branch3"],
 "impl_commit_hashes": {"branch3": "def5678"},
 "failed": ["branch4"],
 "escalations": [
   {"kind": "HARNESS_DEFECT",
    "description_markdown": "The codex tests need OpenAI credentials this environment does not provide.\n\ntest_create_codex mocks codex with sleep because OPENAI_API_KEY is absent; a real fake-codex fixture or credentials are needed.",
    "member_ids": ["tmr-run-test-create-codex#0", "tmr-run-test-agent-types#1"]},
   {"kind": "SUITE_DUPLICATION",
    "description_markdown": "The mngr-list agent-running check was reimplemented in six tests.\n\nExtracted into e2e.assert_agent_running and the six local copies deleted; verified by running all six.",
    "member_ids": ["tmr-run-test-list#0"],
    "resolved_in_commit_hash": "abc1234"}],
 "pull_request_url": "https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/1234"}

Fields:
- squashed_branches: branch names whose test/doc commits were squashed
- squashed_commit_hash: commit hash of the squashed test/doc commit (short is fine)
- impl_priority: impl branch names in priority order, highest first
- impl_commit_hashes: mapping of impl branch name to its commit hash on the integrated branch
- failed: branch names that could not be integrated
- escalations: every escalation you report, resolved and unresolved alike, each one a grouping of the test agents' escalations. Fields:
  - kind: one of "UNCAUGHT_BUG", "FIX_DIRECTION_AMBIGUOUS", "HARNESS_DEFECT", "SUITE_DUPLICATION".
  - description_markdown: first line a one-sentence summary; then the problem, its scale, and what it needs (or what you did about it).
  - member_ids: the `<agent_name>#<index>` ids of the mapper escalations this group covers. Empty only for a problem you found yourself across the integrated diff.
  - resolved_in_commit_hash: the `[NORMALIZE]` commit that fixed it. Present ONLY when you fixed and verified it -- its presence is what marks the group resolved. Omit it otherwise.
  A suite-wide cleanup you applied is a resolved escalation you raised to yourself, so it belongs here too; there is no separate normalizations field.
- pull_request_url: URL of the pull request you opened.
- pull_request_error: present only if opening the PR failed; describe what went wrong.

Then, finally, publish the outputs archive. Run this from the git repo root:

{{ publish_snippet }}

This MUST be the very last step. The orchestrator polls for outputs.tar.gz
and treats its appearance as the signal that you are done. The .tmp + rename
sequence prevents the orchestrator from reading a half-written archive.

